{{-- The WordPress admin theme's dashboard (`wp-admin/index.php`): Ignite's dashboard widgets, the same the default theme shows, in WordPress's dashboard boxes (`.postbox` with its `.postbox-header` heading). The list widgets (`ListWidget`: At a Glance, `wp_dashboard_right_now`, and Activity, `wp_dashboard_recent_posts`) fill the first column, each row as WordPress lists it (a value such as the date first, then the label or its link); the form widgets (`FormWidget`: Quick Draft, `wp_dashboard_quick_press`) fill the second, posting to their resource's create with their hidden values and the way back, as Ignite's widget does (a refused save shows each message under its field, as Ignite 0.6.8's widget does), and with the widget's rows, when it has any, under the form as Quick Draft's "Your Recent Drafts" (the place stays empty without them). At a Glance's rows show WordPress's Dashicons, chosen by the screen each row links to. The stat cards (`StatsOverviewWidget`) are not shown: WordPress has no such cards, and At a Glance gives the same counts. --}}@extends('ignite::layouts.app')

